{
  "id": "COMPOUND:19392 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether is implicated in targeting multiple molecular entities that ultimately lead to the interaction with SMMC-7721. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for MIP, which in turn is targeted by additional compounds, including 7-Hydroxy-6-(2-(R)-Hydroxy-3-Methylbut-3-Enyl)Coumarin and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. These intermediates are all linked to SMMC-7721 through a series of molecular interactions, indicating a potential pathway where Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether may exert its effects via these targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism involving the modulation of scavenger receptors and the activation of signaling pathways that ultimately influence the behavior of SMMC-7721. The evidence supports a role for Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether in modulating cellular processes that are relevant to SMMC-7721, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
